{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/analytical-methods/chromatography/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/analytical-methods/chromatography.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Chromatography | Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-4\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/analytical-methods/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Analytical Methods</a></nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -flask text-purple-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Chromatography\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">A separation technique used to separate and analyze mixtures based on their different affinities for a stationary and mobile phase.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"bg-purple-50 border-l-4 border-purple-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Explain the principles of chromatography</li>\n          <li>• Describe paper chromatography and thin-layer chromatography (TLC)</li>\n          <li>• Calculate Rf values and interpret chromatograms</li>\n          <li>• Explain applications of chromatography in analysis</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1 -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is Chromatography?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\"><strong class=\"text-purple-600\">Chromatography</strong> is a technique used to separate the components of a mixture based on their different rates of movement through a stationary phase under the influence of a mobile phase.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -stop mr-2\" data-mi=\"stop\">stop</span>Stationary Phase</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">The phase that doesn't move. Components can adsorb (stick) to this phase.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Examples: Paper, silica gel, alumina</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -water mr-2\" data-mi=\"water\">water</span>Mobile Phase</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">The phase that moves through/over the stationary phase, carrying components.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Examples: Solvents like water, ethanol, propanone</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Key Principle</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Components with <strong>higher affinity</strong> for the stationary phase move <strong>slower</strong>. Components with <strong>higher solubility</strong> in the mobile phase move <strong>faster</strong>.</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2 -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Paper Chromatography\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Procedure:</h4>\n          <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm\">\n            <li>Draw a pencil <strong>baseline</strong> near the bottom of the chromatography paper</li>\n            <li>Place a small <strong>spot of the mixture</strong> on the baseline and let it dry</li>\n            <li>Suspend the paper in a beaker with <strong>solvent below the baseline</strong></li>\n            <li>Cover with a lid to keep the atmosphere saturated with solvent vapour</li>\n            <li>Allow the solvent to rise by <strong>capillary action</strong></li>\n            <li>Remove the paper when the solvent front nears the top</li>\n            <li>Mark the <strong>solvent front</strong> and let the paper dry</li>\n            <li>If spots are colorless, use <strong>locating agents</strong> (e.g., ninhydrin for amino acids, UV light)</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-red-50 border-l-4 border-red-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -exclamation-triangle mr-2\" data-mi=\"warning_amber\">warning_amber</span>Important Points</h4>\n          <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n            <li>• Use pencil for the baseline - ink would dissolve and interfere!</li>\n            <li>• The spot must be above the solvent level initially</li>\n            <li>• A concentrated spot (small) gives better separation</li>\n            <li>• Different solvents give different separations</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Rf Values -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Rf Values (Retention Factor)\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200 mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">The Rf value identifies components by comparing how far they travel relative to the solvent front.</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg text-center\">\n            <p class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-green-700 font-serif\">Rf = distance traveled by substance / distance traveled by solvent</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Diagram -->\n        <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 300 280\" class=\"w-full max-w-xs mx-auto\">\n            <!-- Paper outline -->\n            <rect x=\"50\" y=\"20\" width=\"200\" height=\"240\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9ca3af\" stroke-width=\"2\"></rect>\n            \n            <!-- Baseline -->\n            <line x1=\"50\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#374151\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n            <text x=\"30\" y=\"225\" fill=\"#374151\" font-size=\"10\">Baseline</text>\n            \n            <!-- Solvent front -->\n            <line x1=\"50\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,3\"></line>\n            <text x=\"255\" y=\"55\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"10\">Solvent front</text>\n            \n            <!-- Spots -->\n            <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"220\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n            <circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"220\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n            \n            <!-- Moved spots -->\n            <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n            <circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n            \n            <!-- Distance arrows -->\n            <line x1=\"270\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#374151\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line>\n            <line x1=\"265\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"275\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#374151\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line>\n            <line x1=\"265\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"275\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#374151\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line>\n            <text x=\"280\" y=\"140\" fill=\"#374151\" font-size=\"9\" transform=\"rotate(90, 280, 140)\">Solvent distance</text>\n            \n            <!-- Component distances -->\n            <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line>\n            <text x=\"5\" y=\"185\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"8\">d₁</text>\n            <line x1=\"20\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#22c55e\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line>\n            <text x=\"5\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#22c55e\" font-size=\"8\">d₂</text>\n          </svg>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -info-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"info\">info</span>About Rf Values</h4>\n          <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n            <li>• Rf values are always between <strong>0 and 1</strong></li>\n            <li>• Rf value is <strong>characteristic</strong> for a substance in a given solvent</li>\n            <li>• Compare Rf values with known substances to identify components</li>\n            <li>• Rf depends on the solvent used - always specify the solvent!</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Types of Chromatography -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Types of Chromatography\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\">Paper Chromatography</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Stationary phase:</strong> Paper (cellulose)<br>\n            <strong>Mobile phase:</strong> Solvent<br>\n            <strong>Use:</strong> Separating dyes, amino acids, sugars</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">Thin Layer Chromatography (TLC)</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Stationary phase:</strong> Silica gel or alumina on glass/plastic plate<br>\n            <strong>Mobile phase:</strong> Solvent<br>\n            <strong>Use:</strong> Faster than paper, better separation</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">Gas Chromatography (GC)</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Stationary phase:</strong> Liquid coated on solid support in column<br>\n            <strong>Mobile phase:</strong> Inert gas (He, N₂)<br>\n            <strong>Use:</strong> Separating volatile compounds, forensic analysis</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Video -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Video: Chromatography Explained\n        </h2>\n        <div class=\"video-container\">\n          <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/S4Qw5tD1xQM\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Practice -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-purple-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>Practice Questions\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. A substance travels 4.2 cm while the solvent travels 6.0 cm. Calculate the Rf value.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Rf = distance of substance / distance of solvent</p>\n                <p>Rf = 4.2 cm / 6.0 cm = <strong>0.70</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Why is it important that the starting spot is above the solvent level?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                If the spot were below the solvent level, the sample would <strong>dissolve directly into the solvent</strong> at the bottom instead of being carried up the paper by capillary action. This would ruin the separation.\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. State two applications of chromatography.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside\">\n                  <li>Forensic analysis - identifying inks, drugs, poisons</li>\n                  <li>Food industry - detecting additives and contaminants</li>\n                  <li>Medicine - analyzing blood/urine samples</li>\n                  <li>Environmental testing - detecting pollutants</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-50 to-pink-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n          <li>• Chromatography separates mixtures based on different affinities for stationary/mobile phases</li>\n          <li>• Rf = distance of substance ÷ distance of solvent (always between 0-1)</li>\n          <li>• Components with higher solubility in mobile phase move faster</li>\n          <li>• Used in forensics, food testing, medicine, and environmental analysis</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-rose-50 to-pink-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}\n    .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.95);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);} \n    .accordion-content{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height 0.3s ease-out;}\n    .accordion-content.open{max-height:2000px;}\n    .video-container{position:relative;width:100%;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;background:#f9fafb;}\n    .video-container iframe{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:none;}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}